# Code review checklist

Run this before committing or when the user asks for a review.

## Correctness

- [ ] Change matches the requested behavior; no unrelated edits
- [ ] API routes return correct status codes and error shapes
- [ ] Order state transitions follow `orderStateMachine` rules
- [ ] Role checks applied where needed (customer vs admin vs super admin)
- [ ] Mobile handles loading, error, and empty states

## Security & data

- [ ] No secrets, API keys, or `dev.local` content committed
- [ ] Auth required on protected routes; shop scoping enforced for admins
- [ ] User input validated; SQL injection not possible (Sequelize parameterized)
- [ ] Uploaded files restricted by type/size where applicable

## Shared & API

- [ ] New enums/constants added to `@localite/shared` if used by both apps
- [ ] Services tested manually or with clear test plan in PR description
- [ ] Logging uses Winston/logger — errors include useful context, not PII

## Mobile

- [ ] Works with existing navigation and role flows
- [ ] Network errors surfaced to user; logged via client logger
- [ ] No hardcoded API URL (use `expo-constants` extra)

## Docs & git

- [ ] `docs/architecture.md` updated if flows or schema changed
- [ ] `cursor.md` changelog updated for notable features
- [ ] No log files or runtime artifacts staged
- [ ] Commit author: `Abinash <mrabinash2022@gmail.com>`

## Before merge (when CI exists)

- [ ] `npm run api` starts without errors
- [ ] Mobile bundles without Metro errors
- [ ] Lint / audit scripts pass (when added)
